<article class="env-lemma" id="0BTS">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BTS">Lemma <span data-tag="0BTS">58.4.5</span>.</a> In diagram (<a href="/tag/0BTR" data-tag="0BTR">58.4.0.1</a>) the following are equivalent </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
the image of $h'$ is normal, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
for every connected object $X'$ of $\mathcal{C}'$ such that there is a morphism from the final object of $\mathcal{C}''$ to $H'(X')$ we have that $H'(X')$ is isomorphic to a finite coproduct of final objects. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This translates into the following statement for the continuous group homomorphism $h' : G'' \to G'$: the image of $h'$ is normal if and only if every open subgroup $U' \subset G'$ which contains $h'(G'')$ also contains every conjugate of $h'(G'')$. The result follows easily from this; some details omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>